Package: deskwidgets
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libx11-6, tzdata
Recommends: libgl1 | libegl1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxrandr2, fonts-ubuntu | fonts-inter | fonts-noto-core, fonts-noto-cjk, evolution-data-server, upower, libnotify-bin, xdg-utils
Suggests: nmap, docker.io, python3
Maintainer: DeskWidgets contributors <deskwidgets@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/T0ks1k24/DeskWidgets
Description: macOS-style desktop widgets for Linux and Windows
 DeskWidgets puts small, good-looking cards on your desktop — clocks, calendar,
 weather, system monitors, now playing, events, notes, countdowns, exchange rates,
 Docker and anime widgets (AniList schedule, manga clock, anime buddy).
 .
 Widgets snap to a grid (drag them with the mouse), come in three sizes and nine
 styles (glass, graphite, light, colour, sakura, manga, neon, borderless) with
 any accent colour, and each one has its own settings. A widget is just a folder
 with widget.json and widget.lua, so writing your own is easy.
 .
 Runs on X11 and Wayland (through Xwayland); widgets are drawn by DeskWidgets
 itself (one program written in Rust, Lua for the widgets), no other
 desktop-widget program is needed.
